+            # then overflows its ~160px viewport with no horizontal
+            # scrollbar to reach the overflow (scroll policy is NEVER on
+            # that axis), clipping the right column (Temperature/More,
+            # invisible off the right edge) and the last row (Print, which
+            # spans both columns via expand_last) right at the screen edge
+            # -- confirmed via AutoGrid diagnostic logging showing
+            # col=0,row=2 for Print with a colspan of 2, i.e. it gets the
+            # full oversized width, same as the column that's clipped.
+            # A single column lets every button take the full ~160px pane
+            # width instead of splitting it, so nothing needs to be wider
+            # than what's actually available; menu_scroll already scrolls
+            # vertically (Gtk.PolicyType.AUTOMATIC) to reach the extra rows.
+            #
+            # expand_last=False (2026-07-30 follow-up fix): AutoGrid's
+            # expand_last logic (ks_includes/widgets/autogrid.py) spans the
+            # LAST item of an odd-length list across colspan=2 with no
+            # guard for max_columns==1 -- so with True here and 5 items
+            # (Move/Temperature/Extrude/More/Print, odd), Print alone was
